{"uid":"f881ccfd7472b93e","name":"test_in_flight_collision_within_single_sync","fullName":"tests.test_collision_fallback.TestCollisionFallback#test_in_flight_collision_within_single_sync","time":{"start":1795362204746,"stop":1795362204747,"duration":1},"description":"The same-sync, both-new race: two distinct iCloud photos with\nidentical human filename, neither on disk yet. Without the in-flight\ncheck, both ``collect_download_task`` calls return tasks pointing at\nthe SAME plain path; the later parallel download silently overwrites\nthe earlier one and we lose data (CWE-200-ish for a backup tool).\n\nModels the scenario by passing the FIRST task's plain path as a\npre-populated entry in the shared ``files`` set (which is what the\nreal collection loop does between sequential calls), then asserting\nthe SECOND call sees the in-flight collision and routes to a suffix.\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>The same-sync, both-new race: two distinct iCloud photos with<br />\nidentical human filename, neither on disk yet. Without the in-flight<br />\ncheck, both <code>collect_download_task</code> calls return tasks pointing at<br />\nthe SAME plain path; the later parallel download silently overwrites<br />\nthe earlier one and we lose data (CWE-200-ish for a backup tool).</p>\n<p>Models the scenario by passing the FIRST task's plain path as a<br />\npre-populated entry in the shared <code>files</code> set (which is what the<br />\nreal collection loop does between sequential calls), then asserting<br />\nthe SECOND call sees the in-flight collision and routes to a suffix.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_redirect_config_dir","time":{"start":1795362204739,"stop":1795362204740,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":fal